From: SDD sandbox <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spec-driven: add test-cases artifact between design and tasks

Adds a `test-cases` artifact to the spec-driven schema: test cases derived
from every spec scenario (ID, scenario, level, preconditions, test data,
steps, expected result, automation location) plus a coverage table.
`tasks` now requires `test-cases`, and tasks for automated tests name the
test case IDs they implement.

Base: @fission-ai/openspec 1.15.0, schemas/spec-driven
Markers: every hunk in schema.yaml is tagged `SDD-PATCH(test-cases)`.

Apply to the OpenSpec source tree (repo root):    git apply 0001-spec-driven-test-cases.patch
Apply to a project fork of the schema:            git apply -C1 -p3 --directory=openspec/schemas/<fork-name> 0001-spec-driven-test-cases.patch
  (then keep `name: <fork-name>` on the first line of the fork's schema.yaml)
---
diff --git a/schemas/spec-driven/schema.yaml b/schemas/spec-driven/schema.yaml
index 81336eb..bfefdec 100644
--- a/schemas/spec-driven/schema.yaml
+++ b/schemas/spec-driven/schema.yaml
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 name: spec-driven
 version: 1
-description: Default OpenSpec workflow - proposal → specs → design → tasks
+# SDD-PATCH(test-cases): description mentions the new test-cases artifact
+description: Default OpenSpec workflow - proposal → specs → design → test-cases → tasks
 artifacts:
   - id: proposal
     generates: proposal.md
@@ -195,10 +196,66 @@ artifacts:
     requires:
       - proposal
 
+  # SDD-PATCH(test-cases) begin: new artifact - test cases derived from spec scenarios
+  - id: test-cases
+    generates: test-cases.md
+    description: Test cases derived from spec scenarios (steps, data, expected result, test level)
+    template: test-cases.md
+    instruction: |
+      Create the test cases that prove every scenario in this change's specs.
+
+      Test cases turn scenarios into checks a tester or a test author can run
+      without guessing. They are the bridge between specs (WHAT) and tasks
+      (the work, including the automated tests to write). Do not write test
+      code here - only the cases.
+
+      Inputs:
+      - Every spec delta of this change (`specs/**/spec.md`): each scenario
+        under ADDED or MODIFIED Requirements needs at least one test case.
+        Scenarios under REMOVED Requirements need none; list the existing
+        tests that must be deleted in the Coverage section instead.
+      - design.md, when present: API contracts, data formats, error codes and
+        limits give you concrete test data and expected results.
+
+      For each scenario, write:
+      - The case that proves the scenario as written.
+      - Negative and boundary cases only when the scenario or its requirement
+        states the behavior (an error condition, an empty value, a limit).
+        Every test case MUST trace to a scenario. If you find behavior that
+        matters but no scenario states it, do not invent a test case for it:
+        list it under "Gaps" so the specs can be updated first.
+
+      Each test case has:
+      - **ID**: stable and unique. If the project config defines a scenario
+        ID convention, derive test case IDs from the scenario ID (for example
+        `<scenario-id>.<n>`); otherwise use `TC-<capability>-<nn>`. Never
+        reuse or renumber an ID once the change is reviewed.
+      - **Scenario**: the scenario it proves (name or ID).
+      - **Level**: the lowest level that can observe the behavior -
+        `unit`, `integration`, `e2e`, or `manual`. Use `e2e` only for flows a
+        user sees end to end, and `manual` only with a stated reason.
+      - **Preconditions** and **Test data**: explicit values, not "valid data".
+      - **Steps**: numbered, observable actions.
+      - **Expected result**: observable outcome that maps to the scenario's
+        THEN/AND lines.
+      - **Automation**: where the automated test will live (repository/path or
+        test suite), or `manual` with the reason.
+
+      End with a **Coverage** table: one row per scenario of this change and
+      the IDs of the test cases that cover it. A scenario with no test case
+      is an error - fix it before finishing.
+
+      Keep cases short and concrete; one behavior per case.
+    requires:
+      - specs
+      - design
+  # SDD-PATCH(test-cases) end
+
   - id: tasks
     generates: tasks.md
     description: Implementation checklist with trackable tasks
     template: tasks.md
+    # SDD-PATCH(test-cases): instruction below ends with a new paragraph "Automated tests come from test-cases.md ..."
     instruction: |
       Create the task list that breaks down the implementation work.
 
@@ -260,9 +317,17 @@ artifacts:
       ```
 
       Reference specs for what needs to be built, design for how to build it.
+
+      Automated tests come from test-cases.md: every test case whose level is
+      not `manual` MUST be covered by a task that names its ID (one task may
+      cover several cases of the same scenario and level). Put that task in the
+      group of the component that implements the behavior, before the
+      implementation task it verifies. Manual test cases go into the final
+      integration group as verification tasks.
     requires:
       - specs
       - design
+      - test-cases  # SDD-PATCH(test-cases)
 
 apply:
   requires: [tasks]
diff --git a/schemas/spec-driven/templates/test-cases.md b/schemas/spec-driven/templates/test-cases.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..69e8972
--- /dev/null
+++ b/schemas/spec-driven/templates/test-cases.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Test Cases
+
+## <!-- capability-path -->
+
+### <!-- TC ID -->: <!-- short name -->
+- **Scenario**: <!-- scenario it proves -->
+- **Level**: <!-- unit | integration | e2e | manual -->
+- **Preconditions**: <!-- state before the test -->
+- **Test data**: <!-- explicit values -->
+- **Steps**:
+  1. <!-- action -->
+- **Expected result**: <!-- observable outcome, maps to THEN/AND -->
+- **Automation**: <!-- repository/path of the automated test, or "manual: reason" -->
+
+## Gaps
+
+<!-- Behavior that matters but no scenario states it. Update specs first. Write "None" if empty. -->
+
+## Coverage
+
+| Scenario | Test cases |
+|---|---|
+| <!-- scenario --> | <!-- TC IDs --> |
